<!--
    kuna `option loopcondhoist` (default `on`), P8 goto-quality: the test that
    is a loop's condition is the loop's exit.  The structurers keep the exit of
    the loop's condition block as the loop exit (CollapseStructure findExit and
    the region structurer's refinement), ruleBlockIfNoExit folds that block's
    returning arm last, and ActionReturnSplit does not copy the return block a
    `break` of an unoptimized function shares with the loop exit.

    gcc 11 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none -fno-inline),
    linked with -Ttext 0x100000 (-O0) and 0x100200 (-O2), data at 0x101000:
        struct ent { int type; const char *name; };
        extern struct ent ents[]; extern int nents; extern void *in;
        int get(void *f); int next(void);
        void lookup(int id, const char **group, const char **name)
        { const char *cur = 0; int i;
          for (i = 0; i LT nents; i++) {
            if (ents[i].type AND 1) cur = ents[i].name;
            if (i == id) { *group = cur; *name = ents[i].name; break; }
          } }
        int find(const char **list, int n, const char *key)
        { int i = 0;
          while (i LT n) { if (list[i][0] == key[0]) return i; i++; }
          return -1; }
        int readc(int *c)
        { int ok = 1; *c = -1;
          while (in != 0) { *c = get(in); if (*c != -1) break; ok AND= next(); }
          return ok; }
    (LT and AND stand for the operators an XML comment cannot spell.)

    At -O0 every loop is entered by a jump to its condition, laid out after the
    body.  At -O2 gcc rotates readc into a guard and a bottom test, the latch.

    Pass 1 (default on): the -O0 lookup is the source's for loop (#1) with the
    stores written before its break inside the break arm (#2), find a for loop
    with its return inside (#3), readc a while loop whose break reaches the one
    return (#4), and the -O2 readc a while loop on its latch test (#5).
    Pass 2 (option loopcondhoist off): lookup, find and the -O2 readc are
    `while( true )` with the condition as an inner exit, the old output (#6);
    the -O0 readc keeps its form, because `loopcontinue auto` keeps the break
    gcc recorded with its one return (#4).
    Pass 3 (option loopcondhoist auto): lookup keeps the source form (#1, #2);
    the -O2 readc is not unoptimized and keeps `while( true )` (#6).
-->
